<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><!--
  Foreground layer of VISOR's adaptive launcher icon, and the icon shown on the
  Android 12+ splash screen (see values/themes.xml).

  The VISOR mark: a visor band with an aperture cut through its center and a nose
  bridge swept up out of its lower edge, so the silhouette reads as a pair of
  glasses. Every shape sits inside the 66dp circle that adaptive icon masks are
  guaranteed to leave visible, so nothing is clipped on a round launcher.

  The same silhouette is drawn twice more - keep them in step if this changes:
  drawable/ic_launcher_monochrome.xml (themed icons) and the Compose VisorMark
  in ui/components/VisorMark.kt (in-app header).

  Geometry, in this 108x108 grid:
    band     x 23..85, y 34..74, corner radius 14
    bridge   swept up into the lower edge, 28 wide and 6 deep, centered on x 54
    aperture circle at (54,54), radius 11
    iris     circle at (54,54), radius 6

  The bridge apex sits at y 68 and the aperture reaches y 65, leaving 3 units
  between them. That gap is what keeps the two from merging into a keyhole at
  launcher sizes, so treat it as the floor if the bridge is ever deepened.

  It is spelled as two cubic curves rather than an elliptical arc on purpose: an
  arc would hang on its sweep flag, and getting that flag backwards turns the
  bridge from a notch cut into the band into a bump hanging below it.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="108dp"
    android:height="108dp"
    android:viewportWidth="108"
    android:viewportHeight="108">

    <!-- Visor band, with the aperture punched out (evenOdd) so the navy
         background reads through as the ring around the iris. -->
    <path
        android:fillColor="#FFFFFFFF"
        android:fillType="evenOdd"
        android:pathData="M37,34 L71,34 A14,14 0 0 1 85,48 L85,60 A14,14 0 0 1 71,74 L68,74 C68,70.69 61.73,68 54,68 C46.27,68 40,70.69 40,74 L37,74 A14,14 0 0 1 23,60 L23,48 A14,14 0 0 1 37,34 Z M54,43 a11,11 0 1,0 0,22 a11,11 0 1,0 0,-22 z" />

    <!-- Iris. The Clarity palette's teal accent - VISOR's second brand colour. -->
    <path
        android:fillColor="#FF5FE0D3"
        android:pathData="M54,48 a6,6 0 1,0 0,12 a6,6 0 1,0 0,-12 z" />
</vector>
